! CAM-B3LYP def2-SVP def2/J RIJCOSX TightSCF
# HBDI-truncated neutral chromophore (C12H12N2O2, 28 atoms, charge 0).
# Same basis and same parent geometry as the 32-atom CR2 ladder, so the ONLY
# change is the truncation: the -CH2CHO peptide tail becomes -CH3 and the -NH2
# becomes -H. Purpose is to test whether truncating to the HBDI core moves the
# bright state, which decides whether a future CC3 on this smaller model would
# transfer back to the full chromophore.
%maxcore 4000
%pal nprocs 8 end
%tddft
  NRoots 5
  TDA false
end
* xyzfile 0 1 hbdi.xyz
